      "hints": [
        "Measure the horizontal distance for one complete oscillation on the trace, from one trough to the next identical trough.",
        "Multiply that distance by the time-base setting to find the period, then use the electromagnetic-wave speed in vacuum to obtain the wavelength."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "One complete cycle on the trace spans 6.0 cm horizontally.",
        "The time-base setting is 5.0 × 10⁻¹⁵ s cm⁻¹, so the period is T = 6.0 × 5.0 × 10⁻¹⁵ = 3.0 × 10⁻¹⁴ s.",
        "For an electromagnetic wave in free space, v = c = 3.0 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹ and λ = cT.",
        "λ = (3.0 × 10⁸)(3.0 × 10⁻¹⁴) = 9.0 × 10⁻⁶ m."
